---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import ScrollReveal from '../components/ScrollReveal.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About & Experience | Frankly Inspired"
  description="Franklin D. Parham's background, experience, and impact in nonprofit leadership, fundraising, and organizational sustainability."
  footerVariant="about"
>
  <Header variant="full" />

  <main id="main">

    <!-- ============ PHILOSOPHY / POINT OF VIEW ============ -->
    <section class="section philosophy">
      <div class="container narrow">
        <blockquote class="reveal">
          "Education should not only inform people; it should develop skills, expand access, and create practical pathways to opportunity. Sustainable institutions make those pathways possible."
        </blockquote>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ ABOUT ============ -->
    <section id="about" class="section about alt-bg">
      <div class="container narrow">
        <h1 class="section-title reveal">About Franklin</h1>
        <p class="reveal">Franklin D. Parham is an institution builder, nonprofit executive, educator, and strategist whose career has centered on expanding opportunity while strengthening the organizations that make opportunity possible.</p>
        <p class="reveal">Raised in Alabama and educated at Alabama State University, where he earned both a Bachelor of Arts in English &amp; Communications and a Master of Education in English Education, Franklin began his career close to students and communities. Early work in residential life and TRIO Upward Bound helped shape a philosophy that education should do more than transmit knowledge: it should build skills, develop people, and create practical pathways toward opportunity.</p>
        <p class="reveal">His career has since crossed higher education, institutional advancement, donor relations, fundraising and development, workforce development, alumni engagement, and regional nonprofit leadership. His experience includes roles with Brandeis University, George Washington University, the Society of American Foresters, and The Hidden Genius Project, along with board and advisory service.</p>
        <p class="reveal">Most recently, as Regional Director for The Hidden Genius Project's Mid-Atlantic region, Franklin led strategy and operations across Baltimore and Philadelphia. His responsibilities included regional sustainability, workforce development, organizational growth, financial stewardship, community partnerships, recruitment, participant success, and systems development. He also supported the evolution of the organization's national Alumni Engagement Coordinator model through KPI development, Salesforce operationalization, and alumni engagement strategy.</p>
        <p class="reveal">Across these experiences, Franklin has developed a practical view of sustainability: strong organizations require more than good programs. They need aligned leadership, diversified revenue, disciplined operations, trusted partnerships, useful data, and a clear understanding of the communities they serve.</p>
        <p class="reveal">Frankly Inspired and Associates, LLC brings those disciplines together to help nonprofit leaders build institutions capable of lasting impact.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ EXPERIENCE AND IMPACT ============ -->
    <section id="experience" class="section experience">
      <div class="container">
        <h2 class="section-title reveal">Experience &amp; Impact</h2>

        <h3 class="subhead reveal">Impact by the Numbers</h3>
        <p class="section-note reveal">Metrics reflect Franklin's most recent regional leadership role and are drawn directly from his resume.</p>
        <div class="stat-grid">
          <div class="stat reveal"><span class="stat-num">400+</span><span class="stat-label">youth and families served through Mid-Atlantic regional leadership</span></div>
          <div class="stat reveal"><span class="stat-num">$1.3M</span><span class="stat-label">in combined regional operating budgets managed</span></div>
          <div class="stat reveal"><span class="stat-num">20+</span><span class="stat-label">corporate, philanthropic, educational, workforce, government, and community partnerships built and stewarded</span></div>
          <div class="stat reveal"><span class="stat-num">200+</span><span class="stat-label">student applicants generated through regional recruitment systems</span></div>
          <div class="stat reveal"><span class="stat-num">60+</span><span class="stat-label">volunteers, mentors, educators, and industry professionals mobilized</span></div>
          <div class="stat reveal"><span class="stat-num">100%</span><span class="stat-label">college enrollment among the referenced graduating senior cohort, with more than $500,000 collectively secured in scholarships and financial aid</span></div>
        </div>

        <h3 class="subhead reveal">Featured Experience: The Hidden Genius Project</h3>
        <p class="role-meta reveal">Regional Director, Mid-Atlantic Region (Baltimore and Philadelphia), April 2025 to June 2026</p>
        <!-- Bullets describe the work itself rather than repeating the figures
             already shown in "Impact by the Numbers" above. -->
        <ul class="bullet-list reveal">
          <li>Led multi-site regional operations across Baltimore and Philadelphia, owning programming, staffing, and day-to-day execution.</li>
          <li>Held full financial stewardship for the region, from budget planning through reporting to funders and leadership.</li>
          <li>Developed sustainability strategies using Community Partnership Programming, corporate partnerships, foundation grants, and state and federal funding opportunities.</li>
          <li>Negotiated and established a strategic facility partnership and MOU with the Philadelphia Youth Basketball 6th Man Center.</li>
          <li>Built and stewarded a cross-sector ecosystem spanning corporate, philanthropic, education, workforce, and government partners.</li>
          <li>Recruited, trained, and coordinated a network of volunteers, mentors, educators, and industry professionals supporting program delivery.</li>
          <li>Designed and ran recruitment systems that expanded the applicant pipeline region-wide.</li>
          <li>Helped strengthen national alumni-engagement operations through KPI frameworks, Salesforce data governance, engagement tracking, and systems design.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="subhead reveal">Earlier Leadership</h3>
        <ul class="bullet-list two-col reveal">
          <li>Alumni Engagement Coordinator, The Hidden Genius Project (Atlanta and Baltimore)</li>
          <li>Manager, Fundraising &amp; Development, Society of American Foresters</li>
          <li>Assistant Director, Donor Relations, George Washington University</li>
          <li>Senior Department Coordinator, Institutional Advancement, Brandeis University</li>
          <li>Researcher &amp; Senior Department Coordinator, Wentworth Institute of Technology</li>
          <li>Instructor &amp; Counselor, TRIO Upward Bound</li>
          <li>Residential Life Supervisor, Alabama State University</li>
          <li>Assistant General Manager, American Campus Communities &amp; Clark Atlanta University</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="subhead reveal">Board Leadership &amp; Affiliations</h3>
        <ul class="bullet-list two-col reveal">
          <li>Strategic Fundraising Advisor, Ora Lee Smith Cancer Research Foundation</li>
          <li>Board Advisor, Turner Foundation for Community Advocacy</li>
          <li>Howard Rye Institute Fellow</li>
          <li>Association of Fundraising Professionals</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ SPEAKING AND OPPORTUNITY ============ -->
    <section id="speaking" class="section speaking alt-bg">
      <div class="container narrow center">
        <p class="section-note reveal">Franklin is also open to selected speaking, board service, and advisory opportunities. <a href="/#contact">Get in touch</a> to discuss fit.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ RESUME ============ -->
    <!-- Once the resume PDF is hosted at /assets/docs/, swap the mailto link
         below for a direct download link, e.g.:
         <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/assets/docs/Current-Resume.pdf" download>Download Resume (PDF)</a>
         Keeping a dead/disabled button live on the site was flagged as a
         trust problem, so this is a working interim CTA instead. -->
    <section id="resume" class="section resume">
      <div class="container narrow center">
        <h2 class="section-title reveal">Resume</h2>
        <p class="reveal">Franklin's full resume, covering education, employment history, and leadership experience, is available on request while the download is being finalized.</p>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary reveal" href="mailto:franklin@franklyinspired.associates?subject=Resume%20Request">Request the Resume</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ CLOSING CTA ============ -->
    <!-- This page dead-ends otherwise, anyone who's read this far is a
         warm lead, so send them back into the funnel rather than leaving
         them with only the footer. -->
    <section class="section closing-cta">
      <div class="container narrow center">
        <h2 class="reveal">Strong missions need sustainable institutions.</h2>
        <p class="reveal">If your organization is navigating growth, revenue pressure, operational complexity, leadership transition, or the need for a clearer sustainability strategy, start with a conversation.</p>
        <a class="btn btn-primary reveal" href="https://calendly.com/fparham/30min" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Schedule a Strategy Conversation</a>
        <p style="margin-top: 1rem;"><a class="link-more" href="/#consulting">See services and pricing</a></p>
      </div>
    </section>

  </main>

  <ScrollReveal />
</BaseLayout>
